    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "n minus 1 times: extract the two smallest, x and y, make them the children of a new node z, whose frequency is their sum, and insert z."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "mark_lines",
       "target": "hc",
       "from": 3,
       "to": 8
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The last tree left is the root. With a binary heap, each round costs log n: O of n log n in all."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "mark_lines",
       "target": "hc",
       "from": 9,
       "to": 11
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Why optimal? First, the greedy choice: some optimal tree has the two rarest characters as siblings at the deepest level. Swapping a rarer character deeper never increases the cost."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "hc"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "op"
